/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files
#
# COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE — do not "fix" this. Deployment is `git pull` on the
# VPS, so .env has to travel with the repository. That trade is only safe while
# the repo stays PRIVATE.
#
# If it is ever made public, or anyone is added as a collaborator, this becomes
# a full credential leak — NEXTAUTH_SECRET on its own is enough to forge an
# admin session with no password. Before that happens: uncomment these lines,
# run `git rm --cached .env`, get the values onto the server another way, and
# rotate every secret, because the old ones stay readable in the git history.
#.env
#.env.*
#!.env.example
#!.env.production.example

# Database dumps — api.sql holds real rows including bcrypt password hashes.
# A dump belongs in a backup, never in source control.
api.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

/app/generated/prisma
_parked/

# yt-dlp session cookies — NEVER commit (live account secrets)
cookies.txt
*.cookies.txt
